From 8550c0c17154af2722053daeeca574176ceddc85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:36:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] feat(control-plane): let launchers report running
 instances and close

The control plane needs to tell whether an instance recorded in a run
or in status.endpoints still exists: after a restart, launchers whose
instances live inside the control plane process (in-process servers,
child processes) have lost them, and writing or keeping Ready for them
would advertise dead endpoints to the gateway.

RuntimeLauncher gains an abstract is_running(instance_id), a local,
non-blocking check that returns False for unknown ids, and a default
no-op aclose() that the application calls after the workflow runtime
has closed, so launchers that own servers or processes can stop them.
InMemoryLauncher implements is_running from its running instances.
